<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mary Seacole returns a week after her first visit with her home readings and is seen the same day by Dr. Osei-Hargreaves of geriatric medicine. She took her blood pressure twice a day with the monitor and large cuff the clinic gave her; the seven-day average is 168/96. Her morning headaches are milder but still there most days. She has paused the liquorice infusion, as she chose to, and keeps taking ginger tea. Her knees ache on the stairs to her rooms and when she rises from a chair; the diclofenac gel helps a little. She has not fallen again, but she avoids going out on wet days because she is afraid of the outside steps, and she says some weeks she speaks to few people. She worries about the cost of more medicines. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home readings</td><td>Seven-day average 168/96 mmHg, morning and evening</td></tr><tr><td>Headaches</td><td>Milder, most mornings</td></tr><tr><td>Knees</td><td>Pain 6 out of 10 on stairs and rising</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>None since the one last year; fear of falling</td></tr><tr><td>Remedies</td><td>Liquorice paused; ginger tea; her liniment</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

